{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass on the day it was completed</b> The dedication of the altar is juxtaposed to the blessing of the priests — an allusion to the Hasmoneans, who would make a Ḥanukkah. And further, so that the evil eye would not prevail over their kingdom — therefore He blessed them first. And juxtaposed to the Mishkan — for in the merit of the Mishkan there will be peace. So too David juxtaposed 'YHWH bless His people with peace' to the psalm 'A song for the dedication of the House.'" "<b>And they shall place My name and I will bless them</b> And juxtaposed to it: 'And it came to pass on the day it was completed' — this is 'in every place where I mention My name, I will come to you and bless you.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:21.068338444Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}